c =============================================================
c  Hybrid Office Scheduling - FINAL OPERATIONAL INSTANCE
c  7 employees, 3 functional teams, 5-day workweek
c  Variables : 15  |  Clauses : 15  |  Total qubits (CJ2) : 30
c
c  Constraints: daily coverage + mid-week capacity + per-team
c  anti-burnout (hard); per-team early/late bracketing + an
c  Operations mid-week anchor (soft).
c =============================================================
c
c  TEAM DEFINITIONS
c  ----------------
c  Team A - Engineering  : Manager, Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer  (3 staff)
c  Team B - Design       : UX Lead, UX Designer                       (2 staff)
c  Team C - Operations   : Ops Manager, Business Analyst              (2 staff)
c
c  VARIABLE ENCODING
c  -----------------
c  x[team][day] = 1  iff  entire team is in office that day
c
c       Mon  Tue  Wed  Thu  Fri
c  A :   1    2    3    4    5
c  B :   6    7    8    9   10
c  C :  11   12   13   14   15
c
c  WEIGHT CONVENTION
c  -----------------
c  Hard clauses : weight = 100  (10 clauses, max 1000)
c  Soft clauses : weight =  10  ( 5 clauses, max   50)
c  TOTAL MAX SCORE : 1050
c
p wcnf 15 15 100
c
c -------------------------------------------------------
c  HARD - Coverage (H1-H5)
c
c  Office must have at least one team present every day.
c  Justification: front-desk coverage, package deliveries,
c  visitor reception, emergency escalation, facilities
c  oversight. An empty office is an operational failure.
c -------------------------------------------------------
100  1  6 11 0
100  2  7 12 0
100  3  8 13 0
100  4  9 14 0
100  5 10 15 0
c
c -------------------------------------------------------
c  HARD - Capacity (H6-H7)
c
c  Tuesday and Wednesday cannot host all three teams
c  simultaneously (5-person hot-desk < 7 employees).
c  Capacity is enforced ONLY on these two peak days;
c  Mon/Thu/Fri carry no capacity clause.
c -------------------------------------------------------
100 -2  -7 -12 0
100 -3  -8 -13 0
c
c -------------------------------------------------------
c  HARD - Per-Team Anti-Burnout (H8-H10)
c
c  No team may be in office on all three mid-week days
c  (Tue, Wed, Thu). Three consecutive mid-week days,
c  potentially combined with Mon/Fri attendance, would
c  create a 4-5 day in-office week - a wellbeing risk
c  and burnout pattern.
c
c  This is the hard wellbeing floor enforced for every
c  team uniformly.
c -------------------------------------------------------
100 -2  -3  -4 0
100 -7  -8  -9 0
100 -12 -13 -14 0
c
c -------------------------------------------------------
c  SOFT - Engineering Bracketing (S1-S2)
c
c  Engineering should attend the office in BOTH halves
c  of the week:
c    S1 : at least one of Mon/Tue/Wed (early-week)
c    S2 : at least one of Wed/Thu/Fri (late-week)
c
c  Together these push Eng toward 2+ in-office days for
c  business continuity. Eng leads architecture, code
c  reviews, mentoring - these activities cannot be
c  compressed into a single weekly day.
c -------------------------------------------------------
10  1  2  3 0
10  3  4  5 0
c
c -------------------------------------------------------
c  SOFT - Design Bracketing (S3-S4)
c
c  Same bracketing pattern for Design:
c    S3 : at least one of Mon/Tue/Wed
c    S4 : at least one of Wed/Thu/Fri
c
c  Design needs early-week input for sprint planning and
c  late-week presence for reviews and user research syntheses.
c -------------------------------------------------------
10  6  7  8 0
10  8  9 10 0
c
c -------------------------------------------------------
c  SOFT - Operations Mid-Week Anchor (S5)
c
c  Operations should be present at least one day in the
c  core mid-week window (Tue/Wed/Thu) - this is when
c  vendor calls, budget reviews, and inter-departmental
c  coordination happen.
c
c  Ops gets a single anchor clause (not bracketed) because
c  Ops naturally distributes across the full week and is
c  the team most likely to cover Mon/Fri flex days.
c -------------------------------------------------------
10 12 13 14 0
